          "final_text_tail": "(src/click/types.py:752) registers `ctx.call_on_close(f.close)` when opening files, so the handles leaked \u2192 `ResourceWarning: unclosed file`.\n\n**Fix** in `src/click/shell_completion.py:546` \u2014 wrapped all three context creations in `_resolve_context` with `with` statements, exactly as the PR describes:\n1. `with cli.make_context(...) as ctx:` (main context)\n2. `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_ctx:` (non-chained groups)\n3. `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_sub_ctx:` (chained groups)\n\n**On `core.py`**: no functional change was needed \u2014 the context-manager close protocol (`Context.__enter__`/`__exit__`/`close`, src/click/core.py:468-482) already exists in this tree from PR #2680. I confirmed by diffing against a later upstream release found in the local uv cache (click 8.5.1): its `_resolve_context` is byte-identical to my fix, and its core.py deltas (e.g. `_close_with_exception_info`) belong to an unrelated later feature.\n\n**Verification**:\n- Reproduced the exact ResourceWarning first, then confirmed 0 warnings across 13 scenarios (group/nested/chained, option/argument, multiple, variadic, lazy-write files) with completion output unchanged\n- Full test suite: 614 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed (`tests/test_basic.py` has a pre-existing pytest-9 collection incompatibility, verified on the clean tree; its 56 tests pass with the deprecation warning suppressed)\n- Added a `CHANGES.rst` entry under 8.2.0\n\nChanges left in the working tree: `src/click/shell_completion.py`, `CHANGES.rst`.",
