          "final_text_tail": "at; `None` (default) means no timeout.\n- `Context.close()` (src/click/core.py:641) \u2014 when a timeout is set, cleanup runs in a daemon worker thread via new `_close_with_timeout()` (src/click/core.py:664): waits at most `cleanup_timeout` seconds, then abandons the hung cleanup (\"forcibly terminated\") and logs a warning through the `click.core` logger. If cleanup finishes in time, any callback exception still propagates, matching prior behavior.\n\n**`src/click/shell_completion.py`**\n- `ShellComplete.get_completions()` now closes the resolved context chain in a `finally` via new `_close_context()` helper, so completion cleanup respects each context's `cleanup_timeout` (the value flows through `ctx_args` \u2192 `make_context` \u2192 `Context`).\n\n**`CHANGES.rst`** \u2014 changelog entry added.\n\nVerification: full suite passes (614 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed \u2014 the only pre-existing failure is a pytest-9.2 collection incompatibility in `test_basic.py`, present on the pristine tree; run with `-W ignore::pytest.PytestRemovedIn10Warning`). Manually verified: default `None`, value storage, `ValueError` for `0`/`-1`/`-5`/`\"abc\"`, a 3s-hanging close callback returns in ~0.3s with `cleanup_timeout=0.3` and logs the warning, fast cleanups and exception propagation work with the timeout, no-timeout behavior is unchanged, and completion/`main()`/context-manager/`with_resource` flows all respect the timeout. The `logging` import is deferred into the method to keep the `test_light_imports` allow-list intact.",
